              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for to recycle, then the Russian for to look after."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: условие",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "условие (uslóviye) — \"a condition\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "У меня одно условие: мы вернёмся до десяти. U menyá odnó uslóviye: my vernyómsya do desyatí. I have one condition: we come back before ten."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter. The plural условия also means terms or circumstances: условия работы."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "условие (uslóviye) is built on the old verb условиться \"to agree on terms\", from у- and слово \"word\", inherited from Proto-Slavic slovo (EtymDB). A condition is something settled in words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
