          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "при условии (pri uslóvii) — \"on condition, provided (that)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Я пойду при условии, что ты пойдёшь со мной. Ya poydú pri uslóvii, chto ty poydyósh so mnoy. I will go on condition that you come with me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "При условии, что… takes an ordinary indicative clause. With a noun it takes the genitive: при условии (pri uslóvii) оплаты."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "при условии (pri uslóvii) is при \"at, under\" with the prepositional of условие (uslóviye) \"a condition\", which is built on слово \"word\", Proto-Slavic slovo (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
